2. Precise facts of the case are that the respondent No.1/wife filed a suit against the petitioner/husband for:

(Alif). Dissolution of marriage on the basis of cruelty;

(Bay). Dower in the shape of 15 Tolas gold ornaments or value thereof;

(Jeem). Maintenance @ Rs.12,000/- per month for two months prior to filing of suit and onward till expiry of Iddat; and

(Daal). Return of dowry articles per list annexed with the plaint.

3. The petitioner/defendant/husband submitted written statement and the learned Judge Family Court after framing of issues invited the parties to produce their evidence which they did and after close of evidence the parties were heard at length and the learned Judge Family Court/Civil Judge-I, Lakki Marwat, was pleased to decide the lis in favour of the respondent vide judgment dated 31.10.2018, in the following manner:

a. dissolution of marriage;

b. recovery of dower 15 tolas gold ornaments;

c. maintenance allowance @ Rs.6,000/- per month from 01.10.2017 till Iddat period; and

d. a decree for the return of dowery articles per list annexed with the plaint or in alternative the price thereof.
